# Figma Make → Orbit Sync

## Source of truth

- Design visual/layout source: Figma Make  
  https://www.figma.com/make/4J6d4LW335tDyEDpqq3VD1/Design-Orbit-AI-App
- Product/IA source of truth for shipping product remains `docs/product-context.md`, `docs/ux-design-system.md`, and `docs/technical-blueprint.md`.
- For **Expo Go local visual testing**, prefer matching the current Make tabs and screen layouts.

## Current Make navigation (v4+)

Primary tabs in Make: Home, Tasks, Grocery, Ranking (Ranks), Nova.  
Settings/Admin and Create Task are overlays — not tabs.

## Sync workflow (not automatic)

Figma does **not** push live into Expo. After every Make change the user wants in the app:

1. User pastes the Make URL (or says “sync from Figma”).
2. Agent calls Figma MCP `get_design_context` with `fileKey=4J6d4LW335tDyEDpqq3VD1` and `nodeId=0:1`.
3. Agent fetches the changed Make source files via MCP resources (`file://figma/make/source/4J6d4LW335tDyEDpqq3VD1/...`).
4. Agent ports UI into Expo Router / React Native under `app/` and `components/orbit/`, using Orbit tokens in `constants/orbit-theme.ts` — do not paste Tailwind/web DOM code directly.
5. User verifies in Expo Go (`npx expo start`).

## Porting rules

- Map web Make screens to native: View/Text/Pressable/ScrollView, existing GlassCard / StatusPill / OrbitButton where possible.
- Keep mock-first data via `store/orbit-store.tsx` and `data/mock-household.ts` while testing on Expo Go.
- Rankings live on the Ranks tab (`app/(tabs)/rewards.tsx` route file may remain named `rewards` for routing stability; tab title is **Ranks**).
- Calendar may stay in the codebase but hidden from the primary tab bar while Make is 5-tab; do not delete calendar flows without an explicit product decision.
